{% comment %}
  Root-relative, deliberately.

  This used to be `site.url | append: site.baseurl`, i.e. an absolute
  https://fpavanello.github.io/... prefix on every internal link, stylesheet
  and image. That breaks any deployment served from another hostname: a
  Cloudflare Pages preview would render the new HTML while pulling the *live*
  site's CSS and images, so the branch looked broken no matter what it
  contained. It also made local `jekyll serve` load production assets.

  site.baseurl is "" for a user site, so this yields paths like
  /assets/css/main.css, which resolve correctly on production, on preview
  deployments, and locally.

  Absolute URLs are still correct for canonical/Open Graph tags -- those are
  built separately from site.url in _includes/seo.html and are unaffected.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign base_path = site.baseurl %}
